{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\n`make worktree` computed `target_dir=\"$(if $(dir),$(dir),../$(name))\"`, so with no\n`dir=` it created the worktree as a SIBLING of the checkout. For a clone at\n`~/rebar` that writes directly into the home directory, which is the main source\nof the scattered worktrees this workstation has accumulated.\n\nAn agent filesystem sandbox is now active on this workstation (Claude Code,\nCodex, and Copilot CLI). The home directory root is NOT writable. The default\npath was therefore no longer merely untidy — it was refused by the kernel, and\n`make worktree` failed for every agent session that did not pass `dir=`.\n\n## Situation being documented\n\nThe fix was first committed directly to local `main` WITHOUT a rebar ticket trailer and\nWITHOUT landing through Gerrit, deliberately bypassing the commit gate.\n\nJustification: the broken default was a hard stop for any new agent session on\nthis machine — the first `make worktree` failed, and the failure read as a broken\nMakefile rather than a sandbox denial, which is a slow and misleading diagnosis.\nLanding through the normal path would have taken longer than the window in which new\nsessions started hitting it. The trade was made knowingly.\n\nConsequence: local `main` carried a commit with no Change-Id and no ticket\ntrailer, so the repo root could NOT be pushed until reconciled. This ticket is the\nrecord of that state and of its reconciliation.\n\n## Plan\n\nReconcile the out-of-band commit through the normal path: re-author the change on\na proper branch with a Change-Id and this ticket's trailer, land it via Gerrit,\nand reset local `main` to the landed commit so the root is pushable again.\n\n## Correction to the destination path\n\nThe original criteria named `~/worktrees/rebar/<branch>`. That destination was itself\noutside the sandbox boundary, so it would have reproduced the defect in a new location.\nOperator decision, superseding the original plan: adopt **`.rebar/worktrees/<branch>`**,\nwhich is inside the repository working directory, is covered by `.gitignore` so nested\nworktrees never show as untracked, and matches the 12 worktrees that already exist on\nthis machine. The landed change implements that destination, and the criteria below are\nstated against it.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `make worktree name=<branch>` with no `dir=` creates the worktree under\n      `.rebar/worktrees/<branch>` and provisioning succeeds.\n- [x] An explicit `dir=<path>` still overrides the default.\n- [x] The target's help text and usage message state the new default.\n- [x] The change is landed through Gerrit with a Change-Id and a rebar-ticket\n      trailer referencing this ticket.\n- [x] Local `main` no longer carries the unreferenced commit, and the repo root\n      can be pushed.\n\n## Verification\n\nRun `make worktree name=tmp-verify`, confirm it lands under\n`.rebar/worktrees/tmp-verify` with a usable `.venv`, then remove it with\n`git worktree remove` and `git branch -D`. Confirm `git log origin/main..main`\nis empty once reconciled.\n"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1789780989886802931,"uuid":"a858452c-3426-4d95-89c5-63c9a2d136c0"}